# Local Worker dev overrides for `wrangler dev` (copy to `.dev.vars`).
#
# There are NO app-level Kia credentials. Every user's Kia email, password, and
# remember-me token arrive through the connector's own login form at /authorize
# and are stored encrypted per user in OAUTH_KV — never from this file, and
# never from the repo's `.env` (which belongs to the stdio server).
#
# Nothing here is required to run the hosted connector locally. The only value
# worth overriding is the command-registration ceiling, which `wrangler.jsonc`
# already pins to "comfort" for the deployed Worker.
#
#   none    — no vehicle command tools registered (read-only)
#   comfort — climate + charging only. The car cannot be unlocked. (deployed)
#   all     — also registers door lock/unlock
#
# Leave this commented out unless you are deliberately testing another mode.
# Anything unrecognized fails CLOSED to "none".
# KIA_WRITE_MODE=comfort

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WARNING — `wrangler dev` also reads this repo's `.env`, which the STDIO server
# uses, and merges those values over wrangler.jsonc's `vars`. If your `.env`
# sets KIA_WRITE_MODE=all, your local Worker will register door lock/unlock even
# though production does not. That is a local-dev-only difference (the deploy
# ships wrangler.jsonc's value), but it is worth knowing before you conclude the
# hosted roster is wrong.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
